# The annotations of stage2 (kit/mkgame.py --part src/stage2/stage2.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
#
# TZX block 3, the loader's second stage: 2060 bytes ($080C) loaded to $609C-$68A7 by LoaderStart ($FFEE, src/tape)
# and run from $609C. Witness: c1 (128K) and c48 (48K), both from power-on with the original TZX. "Witness: L1 0 (c1)"
# lines are placeholders the lead's --fix-witness fills.

@equ $4000 Bootstrap ; block 5's load address: the bootstrap (src/boot) starts there, the rest of the screen holds the game's resident bytes
@equ $4052 BootIs128K ; the operand of the bootstrap's LD A,$01 at $4051: 1 on a 128K, 0 on a 48K
@equ $4800 ScreenMiddle 2048 ; the middle third of the screen
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the screen attributes
@equ $5FA9 ToolStep ; a routine of the tape tool TapeWriter belongs to (not in this block; A = 1)
@equ $6B5C Block4 ; block 4's load address (the game, src/game)
@equ $8000 Block6Buffer ; block 6 is loaded here and swapped into bank 4 at $C000
@equ $C000 BankWindow ; the paged bank's address
@equ $FE00 ToolInit ; the tape tool's set-up (not in this block)
@equ $FE4D ToolRead ; the tape tool's block routine of the first pass: IX = the address, DE = the length
@equ $FECC ToolSaveBlock ; the tape tool's save with flag $FF (two bytes before ToolSaBytes, like LoadBlock / LdBytes)
@equ $FECE ToolSaBytes ; the tape tool's save: A = the flag, IX = the address, DE = the length
@equ $FF00 LoadBlock ; the tape loader's block load, flag $FF (src/tape)
@equ $68A8 HeaderTemplate 17 ; a tape header (type, name, length, two parameters) just past this block
@equ $68B9 HeaderData ; the data saved after HeaderTemplate (its parameter 2 bytes)

@module stage2 ; The loader's second stage: the title scroll, the load of blocks 4-6, the 128K test
@about Stage 2 shows the SWITCHBLADE logo and scrolls "COPYRIGHT GREMLIN GRAPHICS 1991 ... LOADING" (Stage2Title), then loads block 4 (the game, $92A1 bytes to $6B5C-$FDFC) and block 5 ($1191 bytes to $4000: the bootstrap, the AY glue and the resident code, into the screen) with the tape loader's LoadBlock, tests for a 128K (Has128K, which also tells the bootstrap), and on a 128K loads block 6 ($20F9 bytes, the AY player and the 128K intro) through $8000 into bank 4. Then JP $4000, the bootstrap.
@about Bank 4 cannot be loaded directly: paging it in at $C000 would page out the loader at $FF00. So SwapBank swaps $8000-$A0F8 with bank 4's $C000-$E0F8 before the load and again after it: the game's bytes at $8000 go back, block 6 ends in bank 4.
@about TapeWriter $60A5 is a leftover of the mastering tool that wrote the tape: never called, it uses routines and a header outside this block.
$609C c Stage2 ; The second stage: the title scroll, the load of the game, then the bootstrap
> From LoaderStart `$FFEE` (`JP $609C`). Stage2Title `$61B2`, LoadGame `$612F`, `JP $4000` (the bootstrap, block 5).
> Witness: L1 2 (c x2).
$60A5 c TapeWriter ; A leftover of the mastering tool: read the blocks, then save the whole tape (never run)
> Not called from anywhere in the tape's code. HL, DE (pushed twice) are a block's address and length (stage 2 itself, by the order). First pass: ToolInit `$FE00`, ToolRead `$FE4D` on that block, a wait (Delay `$621F`, E = 6), then ToolRead on block 4 (`$6B5C`, `$92A1`), block 5 (`$4000`, `$1191`) and, between two SwapBank calls (bank 4), block 6 (`$8000`, `$20F9`). Then ToolStep `$5FA9` with A = 1.
> Second pass, the tape in its order: a header (ToolSaBytes `$FECE`, flag 0, HeaderTemplate `$68A8`, 17 bytes), its data (ToolSaveBlock `$FECC` from `$68B9`, length = the header's parameter 2), the first block (the pushed HL, DE), block 4, block 5, block 6 (swapped through bank 4 again). The same addresses and lengths as LoadGame: this is how the tape was written.
> What `$FE00`, `$FE4D`, `$5FA9` do is not known (they are not on the tape); the names are guesses from the calls.
> Witness: L1 0 (). Not run in the keyed recordings.
$60B2 ; wait about 3 s
$60DF ; the second pass: the header, its data, then the blocks
$612F c LoadGame ; Load block 4 to $6B5C, block 5 to $4000 and, on a 128K, block 6 into bank 4
> 1. LoadBlock `$FF00`: IX = `$6B5C`, DE = `$92A1` (block 4, the game from `$6B5C` to `$FDFC`: just past stage 2, which ends at `$68A7`, and below the tape loader at `$FF00`; the stack is still below `$5D37`).
> 2. The attributes cleared to 0 (the screen goes black), LoadBlock IX = `$4000`, DE = `$1191` (block 5 into the screen: the bootstrap and glue `$4000-$4145`, the resident code `$4146-$5092`, the panel code `$5093-$5190`).
> 3. Has128K `$618E`: on a 48K return. On a 128K: SwapBank (A = `$14`), LoadBlock IX = `$8000`, DE = `$20F9` (block 6), SwapBank again.
> Witness: L1 2 (c x2).
$6139 ; black attributes: block 5 loads into a hidden screen
$6150 ; a 128K: block 6 through $8000 into bank 4
$6169 LoadGameEnd
$616A c SwapBank ; Page bank A, swap $8000-$A0F8 with $C000-$E0F8, page bank 0 and the 48K ROM ($10)
> A = the `$7FFD` value (`$14`: bank 4, the 48K BASIC ROM). DI first. SwapBlock `$617B`, then `$10` to `$7FFD`.
> Witness: L1 2 (c x1). Ran only in c1 (the 128K).
$617B c SwapBlock ; Swap the $20F9 bytes at $8000 with those at $C000
> Witness: L1 2 (c x1). Ran only in c1.
$6184 SwapBlockLoop
$618E c Has128K ; Is there a 128K's paging? Z on a 48K; the answer also goes to the bootstrap (BootIs128K $4052)
> Takes the byte at `$C000`, pages bank 4 (`$14`), writes its complement, pages bank 0 (`$10`) and compares: unchanged means bank 4 is another bank (a 128K, E = 1); on a 48K the port does nothing, the byte read back is the complement (E = 0). The byte is put back; E is stored at `$4052`, the operand of the bootstrap's `LD A,$01` (block 5 was just loaded there), and A = E, Z on a 48K.
> Witness: L1 2 (c x2).
$61AA Has128KStore
$61B2 c Stage2Title ; The loading screen: the logo, then "COPYRIGHT GREMLIN GRAPHICS 1991" scrolls out and "LOADING" in
> Attributes all `$47` (white on black). Logo `$622B` at `$4803` (26 bytes x 48 rows, Blit with A = 6 character rows); Blit's source step (`$620B`) = `$1B`, so a row of ScrollText (59 bytes) shows 32 bytes; ScrollShow, a wait (Delay E = 5, about 2.4 s), then 80 steps: every row of ScrollText is shifted 4 pixels left (RLD from its right end, a 0 nibble in) and shown again. After 320 pixels "LOADING" stands in the window.
> Witness: L1 2 (c x2).
$61CD ; the text window: 32 of the 59 bytes a row
$61DB ; 80 steps of 4 pixels
$61DD Stage2TitleStep
$61E3 Stage2TitleRow
$61E6 Stage2TitleShift
$61F5 c ScrollShow ; Show 32 bytes of each of the 7 rows of ScrollText at $48E0
> HL = ScrollText `$670B`, DE = `$48E0`, B = 7 rows, C = 32 bytes, A = 1 character row; falls into Blit.
> Witness: L1 872 (c x2).
$6200 c Blit ; Copy A character rows of B pixel rows x C bytes from HL to the screen at DE; HL += the step at $620B a row
> The inner loop copies one pixel row (LDIR), adds the source step (the operand at `$620B`, 0 for the logo, `$1B` for the scroll) and goes one pixel row down (INC D); after B rows E + 32, the next character row.
> Witness: L1 806 (c x2).
$6206 BlitRow
$620A BlitStep ; the operand: the source bytes skipped after each row (Stage2Title writes $1B)
$621F c Delay ; Wait E x 65536 loops (about 0.49 s each at 3.5 MHz)
> Witness: L1 48 (c x2).
$6222 DelayLoop
$622B b Logo 26 ; The SWITCHBLADE logo: 48 pixel rows of 26 bytes, drawn by Blit at $4803
> A graphics resource (1248 bytes, plain rows top to bottom; the attribute is `$47`).
@res graphics/loader-logo.bin
$670B b ScrollText 59 ; The scroll's text in pixels: 7 rows of 59 bytes, "COPYRIGHT GREMLIN GRAPHICS 1991", spaces, "LOADING"
> A graphics resource (413 bytes, to `$68A7`, the last byte of the block). Stage2Title shifts it in place.
@res graphics/loader-scroll.bin
